  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The initial TiVNbTa alloy is a single-phase, dendritic BCC material.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial TiVNbTa alloy contains no dispersion particles.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 1–3 vol% nanoscale Y2O3 should be introduced into TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical alloying can be used to introduce the Y2O3 particles and create an oxide-dispersion-strengthened microstructure.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention will produce a uniform dispersion of finely distributed Y2O3 nanoparticles in the BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Y2O3 nanoparticles will remain stable at elevated temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Y2O3 nanoparticles act as pinning sites that hinder dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Y2O3 nanoparticles restrict grain-boundary sliding at high temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hindering dislocation motion and grain-boundary sliding will retard thermally induced softening of TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K, Y2O3-dispersed TiVNbTa will have a yield strength greater than the approximately 330 MPa baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K, Y2O3-dispersed TiVNbTa will have greater compressive strength than untreated TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The strengthened alloy will retain acceptable ductility at 1273 K.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
